## Phase 3 — PWA & Performance

### ✅ Step 8 — Create manifest.json and link it
- [ ] Create `manifest.json` with: `name`, `short_name`, `description`, `start_url`, `display: standalone`, `theme_color`, `background_color`, and an `icons` array (use an existing logo image)
- [ ] Add `<link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">` to every HTML page's `<head>`
- [ ] Add `<meta name="theme-color" content="...">` to every HTML page
- **Confirm before continuing:** "Step 8 complete — PWA manifest added. Ready for Step 9?"

### ✅ Step 9 — Fix service worker cache invalidation
- [ ] Open `sw.js`
- [ ] Change HTML pages to use **network-first** (not cache-first) so new deployments are picked up immediately
- [ ] Keep cache-first only for images (PNG, JPG, WEBP)
- [ ] Add a cache-busting version comment at the top so it's easy to bump on deploy
- **Confirm before continuing:** "Step 9 complete — service worker updated. Ready for Step 10?"

### ✅ Step 10 — Fix the immutable cache header conflict in netlify.toml
- [ ] Open `netlify.toml`
- [ ] Remove `immutable` from the `Cache-Control` for JS/CSS files that use `?v=` query strings
- [ ] Either switch to hashed filenames OR use `max-age=3600` (1 hour) without `immutable` for these files
- **Confirm before continuing:** "Step 10 complete — cache headers fixed. Ready for Step 11?"

### ✅ Step 11 — Fix Google Fonts render-blocking
- [ ] In every HTML page, replace the synchronous Google Fonts `<link rel="stylesheet">` with the `media="print" onload` swap technique:
  ```html
  <link rel="preload" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?..." as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?..."></noscript>
  ```
- **Confirm before continuing:** "Step 11 complete — fonts non-blocking. Ready for Step 12?"

